#### 3.1.1. `[isExtended](#dom-screen-isextended)` attribute[](#api-screen-isExtended-attribute)

#### 3.1.2. `[onchange](#dom-screen-onchange)` attribute[](#api-screen-onchange-attribute)

The `onchange` attribute is an [event handler IDL attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-idl-attributes) whose [event handler event type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-event-type) is `[change](#eventdef-screen-change)`.

When any [basic observable property](#screen-basic-observable-properties) of a `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` window’s [current screen](#current-screen) changes, [queue a global task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) on the [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) of window using the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source) to [fire an event](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire) named `change` at the `[Screen](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#screen)` object referenced by window’s `[screen](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screen)` attribute.

