#### 3.2.1. `[getScreenDetails()](#dom-window-getscreendetails)` method[](#api-window-getScreenDetails-method)

The `[getScreenDetails()](#dom-window-getscreendetails)` method completes asynchronously, queuing work on the window placement task source.

Instances of `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` are created with an [internal slot](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-object-internal-methods-and-internal-slots) named `[[screenDetails]]`, which is created with an initial value of `undefined`.

The `getScreenDetails()` method steps are:

1.  Let promise be [a new promise](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#a-new-promise).

2.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global)’s [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-document-window) is not [allowed to use](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#allowed-to-use) the [policy-controlled feature](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions-policy-1/#policy-controlled-feature) named "`[window-management](#dom-permissionpolicy-window-management)`", then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

3.  Run the following steps [in parallel](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#in-parallel):

1.  Let permissionState be [request permission to use](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/#dfn-request-permission-to-use) "`[window-management](#permissiondef-window-management)`".

2.  [Queue a global task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) on the [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) of [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this) using the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source) to run the following steps:

1.  If permissionState is "`[denied](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/#dom-permissionstate-denied)`", then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

2.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).`[[[screenDetails]]](#dom-window-screendetails-slot)` is `undefined`, then set [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).`[[[screenDetails]]](#dom-window-screendetails-slot)` to a new `[ScreenDetails](#screendetails)` object.

3.  [Resolve](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#resolve) promise with [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).`[[[screenDetails]]](#dom-window-screendetails-slot)`.

4.  Return promise.

#### 3.2.2. Algorithm: Request a window display state change[](#algorithm-request-display-state-change)

To request a window display state change to a target display state targetState:

1.  Let promise be [a new promise](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#a-new-promise).

2.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global)’s [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-document-window) is not [allowed to use](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#allowed-to-use) the [policy-controlled feature](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions-policy-1/#policy-controlled-feature) named "`[window-management](#dom-permissionpolicy-window-management)`", then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

3.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global)’s [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-document-window) is not an [installed web application](https://www.w3.org/TR/appmanifest/#dfn-installed-web-application), then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

4.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) does not have [transient activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#transient-activation), then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

5.  Run the following steps [in parallel](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#in-parallel):

1.  Let permissionState be [request permission to use](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/#dfn-request-permission-to-use) "`[window-management](#permissiondef-window-management)`".

2.  [Queue a global task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) on the [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) of [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this) using the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source) to run the following steps:

1.  If permissionState is "`[denied](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/#dom-permissionstate-denied)`", then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

2.  [Consume user activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#consume-user-activation) of [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global).

3.  Let state be the window’s [display state](#display-state).

4.  If any of the following are true, then [resolve](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#resolve) promise with undefined and abort these steps:

-   targetState is "minimized" and state is [minimized](#display-state-minimized).

-   targetState is "maximized" and state is [maximized](#display-state-maximized).

-   targetState is "restored" and state is [normal](#display-state-normal).

5.  If targetState is "minimized" or "maximized":

1.  Request the user agent to change the window’s display state to targetState.

6.  Else if targetState is "restored":

1.  If state is [minimized](#display-state-minimized), request the user agent to unminimize the window, restoring it to its [display state](#display-state) prior to being minimized.

2.  Else if state is [fullscreen](#display-state-fullscreen), request the user agent to exit fullscreen, restoring the window to its [display state](#display-state) prior to entering fullscreen.

3.  Else if state is [maximized](#display-state-maximized), request the user agent to unmaximize the window, restoring it to the [normal](#display-state-normal) display state.

7.  If the operation succeeds, [resolve](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#resolve) promise with undefined.

8.  If the operation fails, [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

6.  Return promise.

#### 3.2.3. `[minimize()](#dom-window-minimize)` method[](#api-window-minimize-method)

The `[minimize()](#dom-window-minimize)` method completes asynchronously, queuing work on the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source).

The `minimize()` method steps are:

1.  Return the result of running the [request a window display state change](#request-a-window-display-state-change) algorithm with "minimized".

