#### 3.2.6. `[setResizable()](#dom-window-setresizable)` method[](#api-window-setresizable-method)

The `[setResizable()](#dom-window-setresizable)` method completes asynchronously, queuing work on the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source).

The `setResizable(resizable)` method steps are:

1.  Let promise be [a new promise](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#a-new-promise).

2.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global)’s [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-document-window) is not [allowed to use](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#allowed-to-use) the [policy-controlled feature](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions-policy-1/#policy-controlled-feature) named "`[window-management](#dom-permissionpolicy-window-management)`", then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

3.  If [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)’s [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global)’s [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#concept-document-window) is not an [installed web application](https://www.w3.org/TR/appmanifest/#dfn-installed-web-application), then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

4.  Run the following steps [in parallel](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#in-parallel):

1.  Let permissionState be [request permission to use](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/#dfn-request-permission-to-use) "`[window-management](#permissiondef-window-management)`".

2.  [Queue a global task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) on the [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) of [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this) using the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source) to run the following steps:

1.  If permissionState is "`[denied](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/#dom-permissionstate-denied)`", then [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

2.  Request the user agent to set the resizable state of the window to resizable.

3.  If the operation succeeds, [resolve](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#resolve) promise with undefined.

4.  If the operation fails, [reject](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#reject) promise with a `["NotAllowedError"](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#notallowederror)` `[DOMException](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException)` and abort these steps.

5.  Return promise.

#### 3.2.7. `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` attribute and method definition changes[](#api-window-attribute-and-method-definition-changes)

The following `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` attributes and method definitions are updated to return and interpret values relative to the [multi-screen origin](#multi-screen-origin):

-   `[screenX](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screenx)` and `[screenLeft](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screenleft)` attributes must return the x-coordinate, relative to the [multi-screen origin](#multi-screen-origin), of the left of the client window as number of [CSS pixels](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#px), or zero if there is no such thing.

-   `[screenY](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screeny)` and `[screenTop](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screentop)` attributes must return the y-coordinate, relative to the [multi-screen origin](#multi-screen-origin), of the top of the client window as number of [CSS pixels](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#px), or zero if there is no such thing.

-   `[moveTo()](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-moveto)` steps must interpret `x` and `y` arguments to be specified relative to the [multi-screen origin](#multi-screen-origin).

-   `[open()](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#dom-open)` steps must interpret `"left"` and `"top"` feature values to be specified relative to the [multi-screen origin](#multi-screen-origin).

#### 3.2.8. `[Window.open()](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#dom-open)` method definition changes[](#api-window-open-method-definition-changes)

Instances of `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` are created with an [internal slot](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-object-internal-methods-and-internal-slots) named `[[targetScreenFullscreen]]`, which has a data model equivalent to [last activation timestamp](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#last-activation-timestamp). It corresponds to a `[DOMHighResTimeStamp](https://www.w3.org/TR/hr-time-3/#typedefdef-domhighrestimestamp)` value except for two cases: positive infinity indicates that the `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` has never been activated, while negative infinity indicates that a user activation-gated API (see [HTML § 6.4.3 APIs gated by user activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#user-activation-gated-apis)) has [consumed](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#consume-user-activation) the last user activation of the `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)`. The initial value is positive infinity.

The `[Window.open()](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#dom-open)` method steps, and the steps of methods invoked therein, are updated to optionally:

1.  Waive the [transient activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#transient-activation) state requirement when the [current high resolution time](https://www.w3.org/TR/hr-time-3/#dfn-current-high-resolution-time) of the [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) is greater than or equal to [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).`[[[targetScreenFullscreen]]](#dom-window-targetscreenfullscreen-slot)`, and less than [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).`[[[targetScreenFullscreen]]](#dom-window-targetscreenfullscreen-slot)` plus the [transient activation duration](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#transient-activation-duration).

2.  Set [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).`[[[targetScreenFullscreen]]](#dom-window-targetscreenfullscreen-slot)` to negative infinity immediately after following the steps to [consume user activation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#consume-user-activation).

### 3.3. `[ScreenDetails](#screendetails)` interface[](#api-screendetails-interface)

screenDetails . `[screens](#dom-screendetails-screens)`

Returns an array of `[ScreenDetailed](#screendetailed)` objects that describe each of the screens.

screenDetails . `[currentScreen](#dom-screendetails-currentscreen)`

Returns a `[ScreenDetailed](#screendetailed)` object that describes the [current screen](#current-screen). This object describes the same [screen](#screen) as `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)`.`[screen](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screen)`, but provides a superset of the information.

screenDetails . `[onscreenschange](#dom-screendetails-onscreenschange)`

Fired when the set of [screens](#screen) changes; i.e. when a [screen](#screen) is added or removed.

screenDetails . `[oncurrentscreenchange](#dom-screendetails-oncurrentscreenchange)`

Fired when the [current screen](#current-screen) or an attribute thereof changes; i.e. when the window moves to another [screen](#screen), or a property of the [current screen](#current-screen) changes.

