#### 3.3.1. `[screens](#dom-screendetails-screens)` attribute[](#api-screendetails-screens-attribute)

The `screens` getter steps are:

1.  Let screens be a new [list](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list).

2.  For each screen of the device’s [screens](#screen):

1.  Let a be the `[ScreenDetailed](#screendetailed)` object describing screen.

2.  [Append](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-append) a to screens.

3.  Return the result of [sorting](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-sort-in-ascending-order) screens in ascending order with the [screen ordering](#screen-ordering) algorithm.

The screen ordering algorithm defines a [screen](#screen) a as less than a [screen](#screen) b if the following steps return true:

1.  If a’s [screen position](#screen-screen-position) x-coordinate is less than b’s [screen position](#screen-screen-position) x-coordinate, then return true.

2.  If b’s [screen position](#screen-screen-position) x-coordinate is less than a’s [screen position](#screen-screen-position) x-coordinate, then return false.

3.  If a’s [screen position](#screen-screen-position) y-coordinate is less than b’s [screen position](#screen-screen-position) y-coordinate, then return true.

4.  Otherwise, return false.

#### 3.3.2. `[currentScreen](#dom-screendetails-currentscreen)` attribute[](#api-screendetails-currentscreen-attribute)

The `currentScreen` getter steps are to return the `[ScreenDetailed](#screendetailed)` object in `[screens](#dom-screendetails-screens)` representing the [current screen](#current-screen) of the `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` object associated with [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this).

Note: Which exact `[ScreenDetailed](#screendetailed)` object in `[screens](#dom-screendetails-screens)` represents the [current screen](#current-screen) of a `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)` is assumed to be defined by operating systems and user agents. This corresponds with `[Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window)`.`[screen](https://www.w3.org/TR/cssom-view-1/#dom-window-screen)`, the canonical screen for a given window, for example the screen with the largest area intersecting the window.

Note: `[currentScreen](#dom-screendetails-currentscreen)` is guaranteed to be `===` comparable with one of the entries in `[screens](#dom-screendetails-screens)`, to facilitate such comparisons, e.g. `screenDetails.screens.find(s => s !== screenDetails.currentScreen);`. That precludes `[currentScreen](#dom-screendetails-currentscreen)` from being marked `[SameObject]`. Relatedly, `[change](#eventdef-screendetailed-change)` event listeners added to `[currentScreen](#dom-screendetails-currentscreen)` will only be notified of changes for that specific [screen](#screen), while `[currentscreenchange](#eventdef-screendetails-currentscreenchange)` event listeners will be notified of changes for whichever [screen](#screen) happens to be the window’s [current screen](#current-screen), i.e. after the window moves from one [screen](#screen) to another.

#### 3.3.3. `[onscreenschange](#dom-screendetails-onscreenschange)` attribute[](#api-screendetails-onscreenschange-attribute)

The `onscreenschange` attribute is an [event handler IDL attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-idl-attributes) whose [event handler event type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-event-type) is `[screenschange](#eventdef-screendetails-screenschange)`.

When the set of `[screens](#dom-screendetails-screens)` of a `[ScreenDetails](#screendetails)` object screenDetails changes, [queue a global task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-a-global-task) on the [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#concept-relevant-global) of screenDetails using the [window placement task source](#window-placement-task-source) to [fire an event](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire) named `screenschange` at screenDetails.

#### 3.3.4. `[oncurrentscreenchange](#dom-screendetails-oncurrentscreenchange)` attribute[](#api-screendetails-oncurrentscreenchange-attribute)

The `oncurrentscreenchange` attribute is an [event handler IDL attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-idl-attributes) whose [event handler event type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-handler-event-type) is `[currentscreenchange](#eventdef-screendetails-currentscreenchange)`.


